course: dictionary
lesson: 11947
title: Fizzy words: carbonated
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are hard to read, but the words around them often give clues. «Sam's carbonated lemonade fizzed loudly when he opened the bottle.» The word fizzed is a clue, so carbonated must describe a drink that fizzes.
explain: Carbonated is an adjective, a word that describes a thing. It tells you what kind of drink it is. Everyday words for it include fizzy (UK), sparkling, soda or pop (US), and soft drink, depending on where you live.
explain: Carbonate is also a verb, meaning to add carbon dioxide gas to a liquid. «The factory carbonated the water before it went into the bottles» means gas was put into the water.
fact: Carbonated means having bubbles of carbon dioxide gas in it, so it is fizzy.
fact: «Carbonated water» is water with bubbles of gas in it.
fact: In science, a carbonated drink has gas dissolved in the liquid. When you open the bottle, the pressure drops and the bubbles escape.
fact: In health lessons, many carbonated drinks are talked about because they often have lots of sugar, which is bad for teeth.
fact: Carbonate, carbonates, carbonated and carbonating are all forms of the same verb, meaning to add carbon dioxide to a liquid.
exercise: «Sam's carbonated lemonade fizzed loudly when he opened it.» What does carbonated mean? | Cold, straight from the freezer | Sweet and sticky like honey | *Fizzy, with bubbles of gas in it | Made from apples only
exercise: In science, a carbonated drink has a gas dissolved in it. What gas is it? | Oxygen | Hydrogen | *Carbon dioxide | Helium
exercise: Which everyday word is used in the UK for a carbonated drink? | Frozen | Quiet | Thick | *Fizzy
test: «Mia carbonated the water by adding carbon dioxide.» In this sentence, what does carbonated mean? | Poured the water into a glass | *Added carbon dioxide gas to the water | Boiled the water until it was hot | Froze the water into ice
test: Ben says many soft drinks are carbonated. Why might a health lesson talk about them? | They are always cold | They taste of medicine | Their bottles are too heavy | *Many have lots of sugar, which is bad for teeth
exam: Which sentence uses carbonated correctly? | The carbonated dog ran in the park | *The carbonated lemonade fizzed when I opened it | The carbonated bus drove to school | The carbonated sandwich was warm and tasty
